Architecture plan

Scope reviewed
- Issue #1: Initialize repo and HTML skeleton.
- PRODUCT.md is not present, and the issue does not define a product brand/name, so no additional brand naming should be introduced.

Module structure and file organization
- Keep the project as a minimal static site.
- Root files:
  - index.html: semantic HTML document with head metadata, title, body landmark structure, and a stylesheet link.
  - styles.css: empty or minimal stylesheet stub linked from index.html.
  - README.md: existing project readme.

Shared types and modules
- None. This issue does not require JavaScript, generated assets, package tooling, or shared application types.

Dependencies between issues
- Issue #1 is the foundation for any later UI or styling work because it establishes the root HTML entry point and CSS file.
- Later issues should build on the static file structure unless they explicitly introduce a framework or build tool.

Key design decisions
- Use plain HTML and CSS because the current scope is static boilerplate and no tooling is required.
- Keep the skeleton accessible and semantic from the start, using standard document metadata and page landmarks.
- Avoid adding package managers, build pipelines, or dependencies until an issue requires them.
